title: "GRAIN: Group-Referenced Analysis of Individual Natural-Language Expression"
message: "If you use this method or code, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "HUO"
    given-names: "Kean"
version: 1.1.1
date-released: 2026-09-03
repository-code: "https://github.com/reiserhhh/GRAIN"
keywords:
  - natural-language-assessment
  - computational-psychometrics
  - multilevel-modeling
  - riccati-mobius-flow
  - partial-identification
abstract: >
  A group-referenced analysis method for constructing multiscale individual
  language-texture objects from natural-language behavior. GRAIN integrates
  condition selection, conditional expression, exact Riccati-Mobius continuous-time
  paths, frozen liquid trajectory readers, dynamic multi-time set inversion,
  interaction, reference-relative geometry, uncertainty, and inference-level
  safeguards without claiming a finished scale, clinical diagnosis, or validated
  personality taxonomy.
